## 9. EVERY BUG FOUND & FIXED THIS SESSION

**(THE BIG ONE) The LLM stage never ran — both roles were silently dead:**
- **(a) Sanitizer selection JSON-parse bug** (`src/llm.py`): the old code did
  `content.strip().strip("```json").strip("```").strip(); json.loads(content)`.
  `str.strip(chars)` strips a **character set**, not a substring, and nothing
  there survives the prose llama writes around a fenced block. So **every** call
  raised `Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)`, `fuzzer.py` caught it and
  logged "Falling back to default sanitizers", and the campaign carried on
  looking healthy while the LLM never ran once. → RQ2/RQ3 had **no evidence**
  behind them. **Fixed:** new `_extract_json()` (fence-aware, prose-tolerant,
  brace-balanced with string-literal + escape awareness) + `_coerce_text()`
  (flattens content-block lists); 3 retries with a sharper re-ask; backend JSON
  mode (`response_format={"type":"json_object"}`) with auto-downgrade if the
  backend rejects it; hallucinated sanitizer names dropped **and counted**; the
  old code also fell off the end returning `None` on a shape-check failure — now
  always returns or raises. Unit-tested against the verbatim llama3.1:8b reply
  from the failing log + 9 other shapes.
- **(b) Seed generation dead**: `src/seed_bank/` was **deleted in commit
  87d8602** ("latest edit", which also removed `src/predefined_seeds/`,
  `dictionaries/`, `configs/`). `_load_seed_bank()` returned `{}` so
  `generate_seeds()` short-circuited to `_local_fallback_mapping()` on every
  tool. **Restored** seed_bank from commit `b1b657e` (6 categories).
  **STILL MISSING: `src/predefined_seeds/`** (the create_pdf/docx/zip
  tool-calling seed path writes there; `file_manager.py` reads
  `predefined_seed:<name>`). Decide: restore it too, or drop the binary-seed
  claim from the paper.
- **(c) `'NoneType' object is not callable`**: `llm.py` caught `ImportError` and
  set `ChatOpenAI=None`, so a missing/half-installed `langchain_openai` surfaced
  400 lines later as a `TypeError`. **Fixed:** now raises at construction with the
  original ImportError attached.

**(THE SECOND SILENT ONE) `run_eval.py` counted findings by strings the reporter
never prints** (`"sanitizer triggered"`, `"violation"`, …). The real
`ConsoleVulnerabilityReporter` (`src/reporters.py`) prints `POTENTIAL
VULNERABILITY / BUG FOUND` and `-> Triggered Sanitizers : [...]`, and `fuzzer.py`
prints `Silent Bug Alert: Sanitizers [...] flagged ...`. So even after the LLM
fix, a **genuine finding would have logged `finding_hits=0`.** **Fixed:** counts
